{title: King of Gath}
{subtitle: 1 Samuel 21:10–15; 27:1–7; 27:8–12; 28:1–2; 29:1–11; 1 Kings 2:39–40}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
David fled the king of Israel
[Eb]Crossed the bor[F]der to Gath's [Bb]gate
[Eb]Achish sat upon his throne
[F]But the servants knew his [Gm]name
They sang of David's fame
[Eb]Saul struck [F]thousands, Da[Bb]vid [Eb]ten
David's heart was filled with fear
[F]He knew his days were [Gm]done
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Madman make marks on the [F]door
[Gm]Spittle runs down your [Eb]beard
[Bb]Why bring such a fool to [F]me
Look at him, he is [Gm]mad
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Six hundred men with him came
[Eb]Two wives [F]in his house[Bb]hold
[Eb]Ziklag was given that [F]day
Saul stopped his [Gm]search
David raided the south
[Eb]Geshurites and [F]Amale[Bb]kites
[Eb]He told the king it [F]was Judah
Deception in his [Gm]eyes
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Gm] | [Eb] | [F] | [Gm] | ×2
| [Gm] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Bodyguard for [F]life he said
March with me against Is[Gm]rael
But the rulers said no
[Eb]Send [F]the Hebrew back away
[Gm]Trust was broken in the court
[Eb]Da[F]vid left with heavy [Gm]heart
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]Two slaves ran to [F]Gath
[Gm]Shimei broke his oath to Solomon
[Eb]Achish son of Maacah
[F]King of [Gm]Gath, [F]the [Eb]end
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Eb] |
| [Gm] | ×8
